COMS221 Operating Systems Labs – Student Setup
===============================================

Follow these steps once to create your own private repository for the OS labs.
The master repository is:
https://github.com/Sussex-County-Community-College/coms221-xv6-labs-fa25.git

------------------------------------------------------------
1. Prerequisites
------------------------------------------------------------
- A GitHub account (https://github.com).

------------------------------------------------------------
2. Clone the Master Repository
------------------------------------------------------------
First, clone the public starter code from the master repository:

    cd ~/GitHub
    git clone https://github.com/Sussex-County-Community-College/coms221-xv6-labs-fa25.git
    cd coms221-xv6-labs-fa25

All setup scripts are located in the root directory of the cloned repository.
Run them from here.

------------------------------------------------------------
3. Install GitHub CLI (gh)
------------------------------------------------------------
The "gh" tool lets the script create private repositories and add the instructor
as a collaborator automatically.

From inside the cloned repository, run:

    chmod +x install_gh_cli.sh
    ./install_gh_cli.sh

After installation, authenticate with GitHub (if prompted):

    gh auth login

Choose:
- GitHub.com
- HTTPS
- Yes to browser login (or copy-paste the code shown).

------------------------------------------------------------
4. Create Your Private Repository
------------------------------------------------------------
From the repository root, run:

    chmod +x create_student_repo.sh
    ./create_student_repo.sh

The script will ask for:
- Your GitHub username.
- A name for your private repository (press Enter for default).
- Confirmation to create the private repo.

It will automatically:
- Create the private repo under your account.
- Push all branches and tags.
- Add the instructor as a collaborator (write access).

------------------------------------------------------------
5. Work on Assignments
------------------------------------------------------------
Each lab is on its own branch. For example, to start Lab 1:

    git checkout util

After making changes:

    git add .
    git commit -m "Completed util lab"
    git push

Preferably, you should use the GitHub Desktop application to manage your repository.

------------------------------------------------------------
6. Need Help?
------------------------------------------------------------
- If you see "gh: command not found", run ./install_gh_cli.sh again from the
  repository root.
- Make sure you are logged into GitHub via gh auth login.
- If the repo creation fails, you can manually create a private repo on GitHub
  and set it as the origin.

